-- CA_0174_dispute_wrong_committee_links_la_unified_b.sql
-- Mark 327 WRONG campaign-finance committee links as 'disputed'. Each sits on one of the 178 placeholder
-- politician rows that CA_0156 classed B NO EVIDENCE (LA County unified school boards; seeded by the unsourced
-- school-district pass, deactivated by CA_0156) and was auto-linked by SURNAME, so the committee belongs to
-- someone else. Follow-up to CA_0156 and CA_0169; same pattern as CA_0166 (four links on CA_0159 rows).
--
-- SCOPE: every 'confirmed' or 'needs_research' link on the 178 rows -- 328 links (1 confirmed, 327 needs_research)
-- on 63 of the rows; the other rows carry none, or only 'not_applicable'. 327 are disputed here; 1 is left
-- as it is (below). The 1,166 'not_applicable' links on these rows are untouched. The disputed links were made by
-- confirm-cal-access.ts (323 cal_access) and relink-socrata-skipped.ts (4 la_socrata), on the surname alone
-- (302) or on the full name with nothing else (25).
--
-- Per-link table, with the official committee name, filer phone, basis and reason:
--   data/roster-audits/2026-09-23-la-unified-b-committee-links-CA_0174.csv
--
-- EVIDENCE (fetched 2026-09-23):
--   * Cal-Access committee detail page for all 324 cal_access filers: official name, filer phone, status.
--     Control filer 1414018 returned "NEWSOM FOR CALIFORNIA GOVERNOR 2022" before and after the run.
--   * LA City Ethics contributions dataset (data.lacity.org m6g2-gc6c) cand_name / seat_desc for the 4 la_socrata
--     links and for 2 cal_access filers: Jeneen Robinson (LAUSD BD4 2013), Elisa Avalos (LA CD7 2022, on 2 rows),
--     Darian Chin (LA CD13 2005), Fidencio Gallardo (LAUSD BD5 2019 and 2024).
--   * LA County RR/CC school-board candidate lists 2017-2026, and the Smart Voter LA County school pages for
--     2003-11-04, 2005-11-08 and 2009-11-03 (Wayback).
--
-- BASIS (the CSV column 'basis'):
--   A   48  the committee names another person, or the "surname" hit is a place name (Corona, Alum Rock,
--              Paso Robles) or a different compound surname (Mc Kay, Mc Shane, Di Donato, Burke Montez).
--   B  248  the committee is for another office or another named district (council, Assembly, judge, a
--              different school district, a college board ...), not for the row's board.
--   C   31  a school-board or unnamed committee that the evidence places elsewhere: the filer phone matches
--              the same filer's committee for another district (Grossman -> Sweetwater, Horner -> Morgan Hill),
--              the county candidate lists name a different person for that surname and year (Robles 2018,
--              Saldana 2020/2024, Escobedo 2005/2009, Kim 2022/2026), the board does not elect that year (Redondo
--              Beach USD elects in March of odd years), or the filer is outside LA County and nothing ties it to the row.
--
-- LEFT ALONE -- 1 link: cal_access 1303021 "ROCK" on Michael Rock (Torrance Unified) stays 'needs_research'. The
-- committee has no given name, no office and no electronic filing in any cycle, and its filer area code (310) fits the
-- Torrance area. Nothing shows it belongs elsewhere, so it is not disputed. It carries no money.
--
-- THE ONE CONFIRMED LINK -- 852ba953 Cheryl Cox (Covina-Valley Unified) -> cal_access 1283795 "COX FOR MAYOR, CHERYL".
-- The committee is Cheryl Cox's campaign for Mayor of Chula Vista (filer area code 619; its 4 contributions, $6,761.00,
-- are the 2006 cycle). CA_0156 recorded it as a lead; migration 1791 kept it because the official name carries the
-- surname and the given name, which is exactly the name-only match. It is the only link here that reaches a read path.
--
-- NAME-ONLY LEADS (recorded in the CSV, not acted on): some committees carry the row's full name for another office --
-- Cheryl Cox (Chula Vista mayor), Eddie Zuniga (won El Monte City SD, 2009), Sue Herbers (Torrance council),
-- Tim Nader (Chula Vista; Southwestern College board, judge), Diana Carey (Huntington Beach UHSD), Jason Paguio
-- (Chula Vista council), George Fuller (Oakley council), Sheila Lichtblau (judge), Michael Murphy (Merced; Michael
-- Patrick Murphy, Sacramento). None is evidence for the row's seat, and each committee is still not the row's.
-- They are the same kind of lead as CA_0169's (Lantz, Fuller, V. Martinez) and go to the same operator ruling.
--
-- WHY 'disputed' AND NOT DELETE OR RE-POINT: 'disputed' is the admin API's own value for a wrong link
-- (campaignFinanceAdmin.ts), as in CA_0166. Every read path and the ingestion scheduler require
-- research_status = 'confirmed' and nothing reads 'needs_research' (migration 1792), so the 326 needs_research
-- links were already inert: disputing them changes the record, so the next research pass does not confirm them,
-- not the display. The Cox link stops attributing its $6,761.00 at once, with no aggregate rebuild. Nothing is
-- deleted: 4 contributions, 1 contribution_summary_agg row and 58 ingestion_runs (on 18 of the links) keep their
-- source. No active politician row exists for any committee's real owner, so no link can be re-pointed.
--
-- NOTES FORMAT: the Cox link's notes are a JSON object, so it gets CA_0166's keys (disputed_by, disputed_reason).
-- The other 326 carry "<json> | UNVERIFIED (migration 1792 ...)" or "<json> | sweep 1664: ..." text, which is not
-- JSON, so they get the same " | "-joined suffix those migrations used: " | DISPUTED by CA_0174 (2026-09-23): <reason>".
--
-- OVERLAP CHECKED: CA_0166's four links sit on CA_0159 rows, none of these. CA_0169 (proposed) writes only
-- essentials.politicians.notes on 99 of these rows, not politician_sources.
--
-- No migration runner exists; this file records SQL applied by hand (pure DML).
-- STATUS: PROPOSED, NOT APPLIED. Operator approval required before the prod apply.
--
-- ROLLBACK:
--   UPDATE transparent_motivations.politician_sources
--      SET research_status = CASE WHEN id = '852ba953-b38b-49f1-bbe2-82ca9c089280' THEN 'confirmed' ELSE 'needs_research' END,
--          notes = CASE WHEN notes IS JSON OBJECT THEN (notes::jsonb - 'disputed_by' - 'disputed_reason')::text
--                       ELSE left(notes, strpos(notes, ' | DISPUTED by CA_0174 (2026-09-23): ') - 1) END
--    WHERE research_status = 'disputed' AND strpos(notes, 'CA_0174 (2026-09-23)') > 0;
-- IDEMPOTENT: the update is guarded on each link's prior status; a re-run is a no-op and every gate still passes.

BEGIN;

CREATE TEMP TABLE _link (id uuid PRIMARY KEY, politician_id uuid, source_system text, external_id text,
                         prior_status text, committee text, reason text) ON COMMIT DROP;
